{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/910962-more-than-human-any-alternatives","id":910962,"title":"More Than Human: Any Alternatives?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-09T10:59:09-07:00","id":910962,"title":"More Than Human: Any Alternatives?","content":"Has anyone come up with alternatives to More Than Human for superheroes-in-the-chronicles-of-darkness? More Than Human is such a damn mess mechanically that I can't really countenance using it. Why?<br /> <br /> 1) XP costs are borked - powers are <i>far</i> too expensive for what they do in most cases. The costs need to be dropped by 1xp for pretty much everything.<br /> <br /> 2) Which brings me to the fact that the mechanics are <i>also</i> borked. Take, for example, Durable - sure, I could pay <i>7xp</i> for one health level... or I could take Shapeshift (Beta) with the Grow and Permanent Weaknesses and the Reduced Verve Cost Extra to get +2 Stamina per Power Level rank for 3xp. The system is scattered with stuff like that, but that's the clearest example.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Hell, Shapeshift is a prime example of how the rules weren't thought through - let me give you an example why.<br /> <br /> Alright, I'm going to make Survivalist Steve - he's tough (Physical primary; Str 2, Dex 2, Sta 4; 4xp from the 25 you get at character creation gives you Stamina 5), and he knows how to live out in the woods pretty well (Survival 3). Now, he has superpowers - namely, he got filled with the Spirit of the Mountain! This gave him a super-strong alternate form. (Shapeshift (Gamma) 1, with the Single Shape and Contingent Activation (While holding the Mountain Spirit Totem) Weaknesses, for 3xp).<br /> <br /> This is where the whole thing goes to shit. Shapeshift (Gamma) gives Steve the following:<br /> \u2022 A free dot in any Alpha or Beta &quot;biological&quot; power - let's pick Regeneration \u2022 with Reduced Verve Cost and Contingent Activation (Touching unworked stone).<br /> \u2022 A &quot;pool&quot; of 9 points that can be traded for either dots of Alpha or Beta &quot;biological&quot; powers or for two dots of Physical Attributes (the other benefits aren't nearly cost-effective enough).<br /> <br /> Alright, so now Survivalist Steve has 4 dots of Regeneration, Strength 9, and Stamina 10. &quot;I dunno, that looks pretty superhero-esque&quot;, you might be thinking... if it didn't cost him a grand total of <i>3xp</i>. I have 18 more xp to spend on neat stuff.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Compare this to the other character I was trying to build recently, Alexandra Chroma. Her whole schtick is that she can &quot;split off&quot; colors from herself as full copies (codenamed Red, Yellow, and Blue). The problem is that her different &quot;components&quot; have different powers, personalities, and competencies. This is <i>ludicrously</i> expensive for someone who ends up being... not all that worth it, mechanically.<br /> <br /> 1) It costs 14 xp to have the ability to split into 3 people (10xp if I take another Weakness).<br /> 2) Variable Array coughs, sputters, and dies when you try to do something like this, so that's a no go.<br /> 3) So we're left with purchasing three distinct powers with appropriate Contingent Activation costs. They have to be Alpha or Beta, and you're getting a maximum of one dot of each. And I <i>have</i> to take that extra Weakness for Duplicate.<br /> <br /> Oh, sure, Red (the Physical component) is easy enough to give powers - but hyperintelligence (Blue) or hypersocial (Yellow) are... kinda difficult.<br /> <br /> If you're keeping track, getting this character up to <i>basic competence in her concept</i> costs at least 19xp, compared to Survivalist Steve's 7xp.And Survivalist Steve is <i>much, much</i> stronger mechanically, since he has 18xp to play with to, say, make himself a rich billionaire playboy with a utility belt (and a mountain costume).<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I'm mainly asking because I don't really want to have to write my own.<br /> <br /> I'm going to have to write my own, aren't I?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-09-2016, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:35:15-07:00","id":911105,"title":"","content":"Where is More Than Human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:45:24-07:00","id":911114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted 